cfg80211: backport external authentication offload for WPA3-SAE

Out-of-tree WiFi drivers hand SAE authentication to wpa_supplicant through
NL80211_CMD_EXTERNAL_AUTH, which upstream only gained in v4.17. Without it
WPA3 is unusable on these kernels even though the drivers support it.

Backport of:
  cfg80211/nl80211: Optional authentication offload to userspace
    https://git.kernel.org/linus/40cbfa90218b
  nl80211: Allow SAE Authentication for NL80211_CMD_CONNECT
    https://git.kernel.org/linus/10773a7c09b3
  nl80211: Fix external_auth check for offloaded authentication
    https://git.kernel.org/linus/db8d93a7a355

Differences from upstream, required by the 3.13 code base:
  - conn_owner_nlportid is added to struct wireless_dev and set from
    NL80211_ATTR_SOCKET_OWNER; upstream gained that field in v4.11.
  - NL80211_ATTR_BSSID is added; the external auth handler needs it and it
    does not exist before v4.15.
  - NL80211_ATTR_SOCKET_OWNER itself does not exist yet and is added.
  - wiphy_to_rdev() is still called wiphy_to_dev() here.
  - enum cfg80211_assoc_req_flags has no ASSOC_REQ_USE_RRM member yet.
  - GENL_SET_ERR_MSG() is not available before v4.12 and is dropped.
  - NL80211_CMD_CONNECT is split out of the shared case with
    NL80211_CMD_START_AP, which keeps rejecting SAE. AP mode offload is a
    separate upstream change (fe4943702c85, v5.1) and is not backported.
  - Upstream also stores disconnect_bssid when taking connection ownership.
    That field does not exist here, and the netlink notifier that consumes
    it is not backported either, so it is left out.
  - Command and attribute numbers are pinned to their upstream values.
    User space carries its own copy of these headers, so appending them at
    the end of the enums would build fine and never interoperate.

Upstream-Status: Backport

